@page "/rendering"
@using TheSingularityWorkshop.Services
@using TheSingularityWorkshop.Workshop.Rendering
@inject WorkshopExperienceService Experience
<PageTitle>Rendering Research // The Singularity Workshop</PageTitle>

<div class="rendering-research">
    <header class="rendering-hero">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">THE WORKSHOP // RENDERING RESEARCH</div>
        <h1>The renderer should be another capability.</h1>
        <p>
            Rendering is a manifestation problem: take a composed Experience and decide how much of it
            must be visible, where it belongs, and which sensory representation is appropriate for the host.
        </p>
        <span class="research-status">RESEARCH SURFACE // NOT A CLAIM OF COMPLETION</span>
    </header>

    <section class="rendering-section">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">01 // THE IDEA</div>
        <h2>Do not make the world pay for detail nobody can perceive.</h2>
        <div class="detail-flow">
            <article><strong>SEMANTIC WORLD</strong><span>Meaning exists before pixels.</span></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><strong>CAMERA / CONTEXT</strong><span>Determine what matters now.</span></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><strong>DETAIL LEVEL</strong><span>Spend computation where perception requires it.</span></article>
            <b>→</b>
            <article><strong>MANIFESTATION</strong><span>Web, desktop, VR, or another renderer.</span></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rendering-section">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">02 // EVENT HORIZONS</div>
        <h2>Proximity should change the representation.</h2>
        <div class="horizon-grid">
            <article><span>FAR</span><strong>WORLD SHAPE</strong><p>Recognize the environment, major structures, motion, and relationships.</p></article>
            <article><span>MEDIUM</span><strong>INTERACTION FIELD</strong><p>Expose the objects and affordances a visitor can plausibly reach.</p></article>
            <article><span>NEAR</span><strong>INTERACTABLE DETAIL</strong><p>Spend the budget on the surface, controls, text, and geometry that can actually be examined.</p></article>
            <article><span>FOCUS</span><strong>PERCEPTUAL DETAIL</strong><p>Give the highest fidelity to the thing the visitor is currently asking the system to understand.</p></article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rendering-section">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">03 // WHY THIS BELONGS IN THE WORKSHOP</div>
        <h2>The architecture should not care which renderer wins.</h2>
        <p>
            A MicroBundle describes a capability. FSM_COS composes capabilities. The host chooses a manifestation.
            A renderer can therefore become one provider in the same larger system instead of becoming the system itself.
        </p>

        <div class="provider-row">
            <div><strong>SEMANTICS</strong><span>WHAT exists</span></div>
            <div><strong>COMPOSITION</strong><span>WHAT runs together</span></div>
            <div><strong>RENDERER</strong><span>HOW it is perceived</span></div>
            <div><strong>HOST</strong><span>WHERE it runs</span></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="rendering-section">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">04 // CURRENT STATUS</div>
        <h2>Research, not mythology.</h2>
        <ul class="research-list">
            <li><strong>Active direction:</strong> renderer capabilities should remain independent of the core composition boundary.</li>
            <li><strong>Active direction:</strong> camera/context should influence detail selection rather than forcing every object to render at maximum fidelity.</li>
            <li><strong>Future experiment:</strong> an AI-assisted camera graph that reasons over semantic scene structure rather than only pixels.</li>
            <li><strong>Future experiment:</strong> mixed visual languages where different composed capabilities can legitimately have different presentation styles.</li>
            <li><strong>Not claimed here:</strong> a finished universal renderer, finished AI camera, or production-ready level-of-detail system.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rendering-section ai-perception-surface">
        <div class="rendering-kicker">05 // WHAT THE AI GETS</div>
        <h2>The renderer can describe what is visible without revealing the world.</h2>
        <p>
            This is the boundary we want to make visible: the renderer reports semantic observations,
            not the hidden state of the simulation. A strategy opponent can therefore receive a changing
            description of what it currently perceives and still be surprised by something outside that perception.
        </p>
        @if (Rendering is not null)
        {
            <div class="ai-observation-grid">
                <div class="ai-observation-card">
                    <span class="ai-label">AI OBSERVATION</span>
                    <pre>@Rendering.AiObservationText</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="ai-observation-card">
                    <span class="ai-label">PROTOCOL</span>
                    <pre>@Rendering.Protocol?.Describe()</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="ai-observation-card">
                    <span class="ai-label">GRAMMAR</span>
                    <pre>@Rendering.Grammar?.Describe()</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        }
        else
        {
            <div class="ai-observation-card unavailable">
                RENDERING MICRO BUNDLE HAS NOT BEEN COMPOSED BY THE ACTIVE MANIFEST.
            </div>
        }
    </section>

    <footer class="rendering-footer">
        <a href="about-us">UNDERSTAND THE ARCHITECTURE</a>
        <a href="explore">RETURN TO THE WORLD</a>
    </footer>
</div>

<style>
    .rendering-research{min-height:100vh;margin:-1rem -1.5rem;padding:clamp(1.25rem,4vw,4rem);box-sizing:border-box;background:radial-gradient(circle at 68% 8%,rgba(0,234,255,.09),transparent 30%),#020711;color:#eafcff;font-family:Consolas,'Courier New',monospace}
    .rendering-hero,.rendering-section,.rendering-footer{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto}
    .rendering-hero{padding:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem) 0 4rem}
    .rendering-kicker{color:#00eaff;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.2em}
    .rendering-hero h1{max-width:950px;margin:.75rem 0 1rem;font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,6.4rem);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.05em}
    .rendering-hero p,.rendering-section>p{max-width:850px;color:#91aab4;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7}
    .research-status{display:inline-block;margin-top:1rem;padding:.45rem .7rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,211,77,.3);color:#ffd34d;font-size:.55rem;letter-spacing:.12em}
    .rendering-section{padding:4rem 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,234,255,.12)}
    .rendering-section h2{margin:.65rem 0 1.2rem;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,4vw,3.6rem);line-height:1}
    .detail-flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;align-items:stretch;gap:.5rem;margin-top:2rem}
    .detail-flow article,.horizon-grid article,.provider-row div{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(0,234,255,.15);background:rgba(3,12,24,.6)}
    .detail-flow article strong,.detail-flow article span,.horizon-grid span,.horizon-grid strong,.horizon-grid p,.provider-row strong,.provider-row span{display:block}
    .detail-flow article strong{font-size:.65rem;color:#00eaff}
    .detail-flow article span{margin-top:.4rem;color:#718e99;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.45}
    .detail-flow>b{display:flex;align-items:center;color:#ff2cff}
    .horizon-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.6rem}
    .horizon-grid span{color:#ff2cff;font-size:.52rem}
    .horizon-grid strong{margin-top:.5rem;font-size:.68rem}
    .horizon-grid p{margin:.45rem 0 0;color:#718e99;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.5}
    .provider-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.5rem}
    .provider-row strong{color:#ffd34d;font-size:.65rem}
    .provider-row span{margin-top:.35rem;color:#718e99;font-size:.55rem;letter-spacing:.08em}
    .research-list{display:grid;gap:.65rem;margin:1.5rem 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none}
    .research-list li{padding:1rem;border-left:2px solid #00eaff;background:rgba(0,234,255,.025);color:#91aab4;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1.55}
    .research-list strong{color:#eafcff}
    .ai-observation-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem;margin-top:1.5rem}.ai-observation-card{min-width:0;padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(0,234,255,.18);background:rgba(0,234,255,.025)}.ai-observation-card.unavailable{color:#ffd34d}.ai-label{display:block;color:#00eaff;font-size:.55rem;letter-spacing:.16em;margin-bottom:.6rem}.ai-observation-card pre{margin:0;white-space:pre-wrap;color:#c8d9df;font:500 .72rem/1.55 Consolas,'Courier New',monospace}
    .rendering-footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:2rem 0 4rem}
    .rendering-footer a{color:#00eaff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.58rem;letter-spacing:.1em}
    .rendering-footer a:hover{color:#ff2cff}
    @@media(max-width:900px){.detail-flow{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.detail-flow>b{display:none}.horizon-grid,.provider-row{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
    @@media(max-width:560px){.horizon-grid,.provider-row,.detail-flow,.ai-observation-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.rendering-section{padding:2.8rem 0}}
</style>

@code {
    private RenderingMicroBundle? Rendering =>
        Experience.HubRuntimeAssemblies.TryGetValue("Rendering", out var assembly) &&
        assembly.TryGetBundle<RenderingMicroBundle>(RenderingMicroBundle.BundleId, out var bundle)
            ? bundle
            : null;
}
